the confusion continues and so too does  the rapid change of leadership  Wanda Vasquez being sworn in as Puerto  Rico's new governor she had previously  said she didn't even want the job but as  justice minister she's next in line of  succession and was obligated to take it  I saw my car gonna go in the water I'm  taking this job as your governor at this  historic moment without ever having any  political aspirations but now with the  firm desire to complete my mission  to serve the people in the best way I  can she replaces Pedro Pierluisi who  took office on Friday he served as  governor for just five days before the  Supreme Court ruled his swearing-in  unconstitutional because he wasn't  confirmed by the Senate massive street  protests forced Pierre Louis's  predecessor Ricardo Rocio to resign amid  a scandal involving his bolger text  messages and allegations of corruption  so it's the third governor in six days  was sworn in it was clear many Puerto  Ricans still are not happy what do you  think of the new governor Wanda Vasquez  I think it is a bad person when she was  the Secretary of Justice a lot of people  die they don't have the resources and a  lot of resources got lost so she didn't  do anything and I'm concerned about she  getting the position because she's part  of the Ricky Rozay administration and  the corruption it will be on the  Fortaleza in in all of Puerto Rico I  mean she don't shine don't change  anything that is a sentiment felt by  many here some say they will not settle  for this new governor no I'm gonna stay  on the three protesting because I think  it's my duty I think it's my duty and if  I want change I have to be part of it  Puerto Rico is an island of 3 million  people and a territory of the United  States it's going through its worst  financial crisis ever and it's still  trying to recover from a devastating  hurricane two years ago that left much  of the island without power  for many months the political  uncertainty now is not making matters  any better the people will have to wait  a while longer to pick their own  governor elections aren't scheduled  until November next year  Gabriel Sandow al Jazeera San Juan  Puerto Rico
 

